          %h2#idea  Idea
          %p
            In the study of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/recursion+schemes"} recursion schemes
            %em catamorphism
            is the simple case of a
            %em fold
            over an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inductive+type"} inductive
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/data+type"} data type
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theoretic
            terms, this is simply the unique
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
            out of an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+algebra"} initial algebra
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Given an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endofunctor"} endofunctor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            such that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+for+an+endofunctor"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              \-algebras
            has an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi μ
                    %mi F
                    %mo ,
                    %mi in
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mu F, in)
            %em catamorphism
            for an
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi φ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A, \varphi)
            is the unique
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+algebra+of+an+endofunctor"}
              initial
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi μ
                  %mi F
                  %mo ,
                  %mi in
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mu F, in)
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi φ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A, \varphi)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi cata
                    %mi φ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi μ
                    %mi F
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cata \varphi \colon \mu F \rightarrow A
          %p
            From the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+square"} commuting square
            of the homomorphism, we have
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi cata
                    %mi φ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi in
                    %mo =
                    %mi φ
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi cata
                    %mi φ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (cata \varphi) \circ in = \varphi \circ F (cata \varphi)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+algebra+of+an+endofunctor#LambeksTheorem"} Lambek's theorem
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "italic"}
                    %mi in
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathit{in}
            has an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse"} inverse
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "italic"}
                      %mi out
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathit{out}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/recursion"} recursively
            defined by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi cata
                    %mi φ
                    %mo =
                    %mi φ
