          %h2#as_a_recursion_scheme As a recursion scheme
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi μ
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu F
            is an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inductive+type"} inductive type
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/recursive+functions"} recursive functions
            can then be implemented in terms of a catamorphism.
          %h3#example_natural_numbers Example: Natural numbers
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            be the functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mi X
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F X = 1 + X
            so that the naturals
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mo =
                  %mi μ
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N} = \mu F
            are represented by the fixed point of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            (i.e. the carrier of the initial F-algebra). The recursor for the naturals can then be defined by a catamorphism.
          .maruku-equation
